<Chapter id="services-reference">
<h2>Sunken service endpoints</h2>
  <p>Sunken uses service command endpoints addressed by
  <code>(direction, slot, command)</code>. A static build table assigns the
  FourCC-like service labels.</p>
  <div id="payload-notation" class="payload-notation">
    <h3>Payload notation</h3>
    <p>Each block describes the route and its payload in wire order. Named types
    link to their entries in the <a href="#type-registry">Sunken type registry</a>.</p>
    <div class="notation-guide">
      <div><code>struct Name</code><span>fields appear in the displayed order</span></div>
      <div><code>type Name = Array&lt;T&gt; &lbrace; … &rbrace;</code><span>a count prefix followed by that many values</span></div>
      <div><code>type Name = Blob &lbrace; … &rbrace;</code><span>a byte count followed by that many bytes</span></div>
      <div><code>Optional&lt;T&gt; &lbrace; presence_bits: 1 &rbrace;</code><span>a presence bit followed by T when set</span></div>
      <div><code>uN</code><span>an unsigned field consumes exactly N bits, such as <code>u1</code> or <code>u6</code></span></div>
      <div><code>Reserved&lt;N&gt;</code><span>N generated filler or reserved bits</span></div>
      <div><code>Bytes&lt;N&gt;</code><span>exactly N byte-aligned bytes</span></div>
      <div><code>alignment: byte</code><span>advance to the next byte boundary after the value</span></div>
    </div>
    <p><code>count_bits</code> and <code>byte_count_bits</code> give the width of the
    transmitted count. The corresponding <code>count_range</code> states the values
    accepted by the metadata. Field names use snake case and omit the leading
    <code>m_</code> prefix.</p>
    <p><i>Generated order</i> means the struct follows the wire. <i>Logical order</i>
    means the struct follows metadata and requires a generated-order note.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="service-jump" aria-label="Sunken service endpoints">
    <li><a href="#service-auth"><code>Auth</code> authentication</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-conn"><code>Conn</code> connection</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-achievement"><code>Achv</code> achievements</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-toon"><code>Toon</code> identity</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-presence"><code>Pres</code> presence</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-friends"><code>Frnd</code> friends</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-cache"><code>Cach</code> cache streams</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-s2master"><code>S2Ms</code> master data</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-party"><code>Prty</code> party state</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-s2multiplayer"><code>S2Mp</code> multiplayer</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-profile"><code>Prfl</code> profile</a></li>
    <li><a href="#service-chat"><code>Chat</code> channels</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>The entries follow Resume and post-logon traffic. A generated order includes
  reserved bits that the serializer adds. An incomplete entry identifies the
  unknown part.</p>
